Falsifies `file_allocation_table::long_name_assembly::verification::a_run_is_accepted_only_when_it_is_well_formed`.

The defect: assembly skips the comparison of the pieces' checksum with the short entry's, so a run
that belongs to another entry, or to a name since changed, is joined to an entry it does not name.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(piece.checksum(), checksum(&short))`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name_assembly.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name_assembly.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name_assembly.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name_assembly.rs
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ impl LongNameAssembler {
         if run.next != 0 {
             return Err(LongNameError::Incomplete);
         }
-        if run.checksum != checksum(short_name) {
+        if false && run.checksum != checksum(short_name) {
             return Err(LongNameError::ChecksumMismatch);
         }
         let total = usize::from(run.pieces) * UNITS_PER_ENTRY;
